                    <ECUC-ENUMERATION-PARAM-DEF UUID="ECUC:de1ff686-12ee-4ad7-9ec0-6be01bf31f78">
                      <SHORT-NAME>CanIfDispatchUserCtrlModeIndicationUL</SHORT-NAME>
                      <DESC>
                        <L-2 L="EN">This parameter defines the upper layer (UL) module to which the notifications of all ControllerTransition events from the CAN Driver modules have to be routed</L-2>
                        <L-2 L="ZH">概述：CanIfDispatchUserCtrlModeIndicationUL配置项用于定义用户控制模式指示的上层（Upper Layer）接口，它指定了当CAN接口的控制模式发生变化时，应通知哪个上层模块。</L-2>
                        <L-2 L="ZH">注意：确保配置的上层模块接口与实际的模块接口一致，避免通知机制失效；在配置时需考虑系统的实时性和模块间的依赖关系；AUTOSAR CP 4.4标准中，对于上层模块的通知机制有明确的规范，需要确保遵循这些规范以保证系统的兼容性和稳定性。</L-2>
                      </DESC>
                      <INTRODUCTION>
                        <P>
                          <L-1 L="EN">via &lt;User_ControllerModeIndication&gt;.</L-1>
                        </P>
                      </INTRODUCTION>
                      <RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF BASE="ArTrace" DEST="TRACEABLE">ECUC_CanIf_00684</RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF>
                      <LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>1</LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>
                      <UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>1</UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>
                      <SCOPE>ECU</SCOPE>
                      <ORIGIN>AUTOSAR_ECUC</ORIGIN>
                      <POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE>false</POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE>
                      <VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES>
                        <ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-CLASS>LINK</CONFIG-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
                        </ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                        <ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-CLASS>LINK</CONFIG-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-POST-BUILD</CONFIG-VARIANT>
                        </ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                        <ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-VARIANT>
                        </ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                      </VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES>
                      <SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>false</SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>
                      <LITERALS>
                        <ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF UUID="ECUC:568bed3d-0600-9153-5091-16456b341a6d">
                          <SHORT-NAME>CAN_SM</SHORT-NAME>
                          <ORIGIN>AUTOSAR_ECUC</ORIGIN>
                        </ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF>
                        <ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF UUID="ECUC:bf62f394-e708-8f17-4485-2fa6657d9432">
                          <SHORT-NAME>CDD</SHORT-NAME>
                          <ORIGIN>AUTOSAR_ECUC</ORIGIN>
                        </ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF>
                      </LITERALS>
                    </ECUC-ENUMERATION-PARAM-DEF>
                    <ECUC-ENUMERATION-PARAM-DEF UUID="ECUC:239a6399-5602-4010-94b5-039c6223fed2">
                      <SHORT-NAME>CanIfDispatchUserTrcvModeIndicationUL</SHORT-NAME>
                      <DESC>
                        <L-2 L="EN">This parameter defines the upper layer (UL) module to which the notifications of all TransceiverTransition events from the CAN Transceiver Driver modules have to be routed via &lt;User_TrcvModeIndication&gt;. If no UL module is configured, no upper layer callback function will be called.</L-2>
                        <L-2 L="ZH">概述：CanIfDispatchUserTrcvModeIndicationUL 是一个配置参数，用于指定CAN接口模块在收到CAN收发器模式变化指示时应通知的上层模块的名称。</L-2>
                        <L-2 L="ZH">注意：在配置此参数时，需要确保指定的上层模块已经在系统中定义并且支持接收模式变化指示；此配置项的值必须与系统中实际存在的上层模块名称一致；在AUTOSAR CP 4.4标准中，确保该配置项符合CAN接口模块与上层模块之间的通信接口要求。</L-2>
                      </DESC>
                      <RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF BASE="ArTrace" DEST="TRACEABLE">ECUC_CanIf_00686</RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF>
                      <LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>0</LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>
                      <UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>1</UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>
                      <SCOPE>ECU</SCOPE>
                      <MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES>
                        <ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-CLASS>LINK</CONFIG-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
                        </ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
