                    <ECUC-FUNCTION-NAME-DEF UUID="ECUC:06a66545-ca16-4f21-ad87-0e7b360f802a">
                      <SHORT-NAME>CanIfDispatchUserValidateWakeupEventName</SHORT-NAME>
                      <DESC>
                        <L-2 L="EN">This parameter defines the name of &lt;User_ValidateWakeupEvent&gt;. This</L-2>
                        <L-2 L="ZH">概述：CanIfDispatchUserValidateWakeupEventName配置项用于定义当接收到唤醒事件时，是否需要调用用户定义的验证函数来确认该唤醒事件的有效性。</L-2>
                        <L-2 L="ZH">注意：在使用此配置项时，需要确保已经定义了相应的用户验证函数；此配置项在设计低功耗唤醒逻辑时尤为重要；AUTOSAR CP 4.4标准中，对于唤醒事件的处理和验证机制有明确规定，确保配置与标准一致。</L-2>
                      </DESC>
                      <INTRODUCTION>
                        <P>
                          <L-1 L="EN">parameter depends on the parameter CanIfDispatchUserValidateWakeupEventUL.
                                        If CanIfDispatchUserValidateWakeupEventUL equals ECUM, the name of
                                        &lt;User_ValidateWakeupEvent&gt; is fixed. If CanIfDispatchUserValidateWakeupEventUL equals CDD, the name of &lt;User_ValidateWakeupEvent&gt; is selectable.</L-1>
                        </P>
                      </INTRODUCTION>
                      <RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF BASE="ArTrace" DEST="TRACEABLE">ECUC_CanIf_00531</RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF>
                      <LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>0</LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>
                      <UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>1</UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>
                      <SCOPE>ECU</SCOPE>
                      <MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES>
                        <ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-CLASS>LINK</CONFIG-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
                        </ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                        <ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-CLASS>LINK</CONFIG-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-POST-BUILD</CONFIG-VARIANT>
                        </ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                        <ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
                          <CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-VARIANT>
                        </ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
                      </MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES>
