                              <SHORT-NAME>STANDARD_CAN</SHORT-NAME>
                              <ORIGIN>AUTOSAR_ECUC</ORIGIN>
                            </ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF>
                            <ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF UUID="ECUC:4b716c5d-0e3e-9156-5724-30ab7915453b">
                              <SHORT-NAME>STANDARD_FD_CAN</SHORT-NAME>
                              <ORIGIN>AUTOSAR_ECUC</ORIGIN>
                            </ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF>
                            <ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF UUID="ECUC:4ddab76d-6616-8c1e-5fc1-f4b414bb0a2c">
                              <SHORT-NAME>STANDARD_NO_FD_CAN</SHORT-NAME>
                              <ORIGIN>AUTOSAR_ECUC</ORIGIN>
                            </ECUC-ENUMERATION-LITERAL-DEF>
                          </LITERALS>
                        </ECUC-ENUMERATION-PARAM-DEF>
                        <ECUC-ENUMERATION-PARAM-DEF UUID="ECUC:835e1440-d156-40fa-95df-59a1e9611bc5">
                          <SHORT-NAME>CanIfRxPduUserRxIndicationUL</SHORT-NAME>
                          <DESC>
                            <L-2 L="EN">This parameter defines the upper layer (UL) module to which the indication</L-2>
                            <L-2 L="ZH">概述：CanIfRxPduUserRxIndicationUL配置项指定了接收到特定CAN接口接收PDU（协议数据单元）后，上层（UL）模块的接收指示函数的名称，用于通知上层模块有新数据到达。</L-2>
                            <L-2 L="ZH">注意：确保配置的接收指示函数名称与实际上层模块的接收处理函数名称一致；该配置项对于实现CAN通信中的数据接收流程至关重要，需要仔细配置；在AUTOSAR CP 4.4中，该配置项的命名和使用应遵循标准规范，以保证模块间的正确通信和数据处理。</L-2>
                          </DESC>
                          <INTRODUCTION>
                            <P>
                              <L-1 L="EN">of the successfully received CANRXPDUID has to be routed via &lt;User_RxIndication&gt;. This &lt;User_RxIndication&gt; has to be invoked when the
                                                indication of the configured CANRXPDUID will be received by an Rx indication event from the CAN Driver module. If no upper layer (UL) module
                                                is configured, no &lt;User_RxIndication&gt; has to be called in case of an Rx
                                                indication event of the CANRXPDUID from the CAN Driver module.</L-1>
                            </P>
                          </INTRODUCTION>
                          <RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF BASE="ArTrace" DEST="TRACEABLE">ECUC_CanIf_00529</RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF>
                          <LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>0</LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>
